# BindCraft2 — Apptainer definition.
#
# De novo binder design: miniproteins, scaffolded binders, VHHs/nanobodies, antibodies,
# cyclic peptides and multistate design in one workflow. Optimises a binder through
# AlphaFold2, redesigns the sequence with ProteinMPNN, then re-predicts and filters with
# models that were held back from the optimisation, so a design is never scored by a model
# that shaped it.
#
#   apptainer build --fakeroot --build-arg BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR=cu12 bindcraft2-cu12.sif bindcraft2.def
#   apptainer build --fakeroot --build-arg BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR=cu13 bindcraft2-cu13.sif bindcraft2.def
#
# Pick by the TARGET cluster's driver, not by its GPU. The driver caps the CUDA major
# version; minor versions are forward compatible and major versions are not. The upstream
# installer makes the same distinction (`install.sh cuda12` / `cuda13`), and it chooses by
# reading the driver of whatever machine runs it — which on a build node is the WRONG
# machine. That is why the accelerator is a required build argument here with no default:
# an unattended build must not silently pick CUDA 13 because the build node has no GPU.
#
# BindCraft2 cannot run on CPU. Upstream refuses `install.sh cpu` outright, because a single
# trajectory folds an AlphaFold ensemble hundreds of times.
#
# Four things specific to packaging this one:
#
#   1. THE CLONE IS THE INSTALLATION. install.sh performs an editable install, so moving or
#      deleting /opt/BindCraft2 breaks the `bindcraft` command. It stays where it is put,
#      and the venv it builds beside itself is added to PATH in %environment.
#   2. WEIGHTS ARE BAKED IN (~5.3 GB of AlphaFold parameters). BINDCRAFT_WEIGHTS is set
#      before the install so they land inside the image rather than in root's home, and is
#      set again at run time so a job finds them. ProteinMPNN's checkpoints already ship
#      inside the package.
#   3. THE IMAGE CARRIES NO `nvidia-smi`. Upstream files its compiled-graph cache by GPU
#      model, read from nvidia-smi, and falls back to ${TMPDIR}/bindcraft_xla_cache when it
#      cannot be reached — which means a container run recompiles every campaign, about 60 s
#      per prediction shape. JAX_COMPILATION_CACHE_DIR is therefore set explicitly below.
#      Point it at shared storage for a sweep (see %help); the default here is node-local.
#   4. ALLOW ~20 GB OF BUILD SCRATCH. The 5.3 GB parameter archive and its unpacked contents
#      coexist before the archive is deleted, and the accelerator wheels are several GB more.
#      Build on node-local scratch, not on a shared filesystem.

BootStrap: docker
From: python:3.12.12-slim-bookworm

%arguments
    BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR=

%labels
    Maintainer  Benedikt Singer
    Tool        BindCraft2
    Upstream    https://github.com/PacesaLab/BindCraft2
    Version     v1.0.4
    Accelerator {{ BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR }}
    License     BindCraft2 Source-Available (Hosting-Restricted)

%environment
    export BINDCRAFT_HOME=/opt/BindCraft2
    # The editable install lives in the venv beside the clone, exactly where install.sh
    # puts it. Prepending it to PATH is what makes `bindcraft` resolve.
    export PATH=/opt/BindCraft2/.venv/bin:$PATH
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    export PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1

    # Baked-in AlphaFold parameters. BINDCRAFT_AF2_PARAMS would override this; leave it
    # unset unless you are deliberately pointing at a different copy.
    export BINDCRAFT_WEIGHTS=/opt/bindcraft-weights

    # The SIF is read-only and $HOME may be unwritable or shared between concurrent jobs.
    export XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/bindcraft-cache
    export MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp/bindcraft-cache/mpl
    export CUDA_CACHE_PATH=/tmp/bindcraft-cache/nv
    # Without this, compiled graphs land in ${TMPDIR}/bindcraft_xla_cache and every campaign
    # pays its compiles again, because the image has no nvidia-smi to name the card with.
    export JAX_COMPILATION_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/bindcraft-cache/xla

%post
    set -eux
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    export PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1

    # Set by `--build-arg BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR=cu12|cu13`. No default on purpose: see header.
    BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR={{ BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR }}
    BINDCRAFT_VERSION=v1.0.4

    case "${BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR}" in
        cu13) INSTALL_ARG=cuda13 ;;
        cu12) INSTALL_ARG=cuda12 ;;
        *) echo "BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR must be cu12 or cu13 (got '${BINDCRAFT_ACCELERATOR}')" >&2; exit 2 ;;
    esac

    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        ca-certificates git curl wget
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    git clone --depth 1 --branch "${BINDCRAFT_VERSION}" \
        https://github.com/PacesaLab/BindCraft2.git /opt/BindCraft2
    # The .git directory is kept deliberately small by --depth 1 but removed anyway: an
    # editable install needs the working tree, never the history.
    rm -rf /opt/BindCraft2/.git

    # Weights must land inside the image. install.sh honours BINDCRAFT_WEIGHTS, so export it
    # BEFORE running the installer rather than fetching them in a second pass.
    export BINDCRAFT_WEIGHTS=/opt/bindcraft-weights
    mkdir -p "${BINDCRAFT_WEIGHTS}"

    cd /opt/BindCraft2
    # No Python environment is active here, so install.sh builds /opt/BindCraft2/.venv.
    bash install.sh "${INSTALL_ARG}"

    # install.sh runs its own checks, but they are advisory on a machine with no GPU. Assert
    # the two things that would otherwise fail inside somebody's campaign: that every module
    # and checkpoint the package expects is present, and that the AlphaFold parameters are
    # complete rather than a stopped transfer (upstream treats an AlphaFold file under
    # 100 MB as unfinished, and a truncated download otherwise looks like a successful one).
    export PATH=/opt/BindCraft2/.venv/bin:$PATH
    python -m bindcraft.selfcheck "${INSTALL_ARG}" --shipped-only
    bindcraft --help > /dev/null

    python - <<'PYWEIGHTS'
import os
import sys

root = os.environ["BINDCRAFT_WEIGHTS"]
found = []
for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(root):
    for name in filenames:
        if name.startswith("params_") and name.endswith(".npz"):
            path = os.path.join(dirpath, name)
            found.append((name, os.path.getsize(path)))

if not found:
    sys.exit("no AlphaFold parameter files under {}".format(root))

# A campaign uses five multimer models to design against and holds two monomer models back
# to validate with, so anything under seven means a partial archive.
if len(found) < 7:
    sys.exit("expected at least 7 parameter files, found {}: {}".format(
        len(found), sorted(n for n, _ in found)))

small = [(n, s) for n, s in found if s < 100 * 1024 * 1024]
if small:
    sys.exit("these parameter files look like stopped transfers: {}".format(small))

total = sum(s for _, s in found)
print("AlphaFold parameters OK: {} files, {:.2f} GiB".format(
    len(found), total / 1024 ** 3))
PYWEIGHTS

    chmod -R a+rX /opt/BindCraft2 /opt/bindcraft-weights
    du -sh /opt/BindCraft2 /opt/bindcraft-weights

%test
    set -eu
    # Deliberately driver-free, so it passes on a build node with no GPU.
    # A PASSING TEST DOES NOT MEAN THE IMAGE RUNS ON YOUR CLUSTER. It does not touch the
    # driver and does not ask JAX for a device, so neither the driver gate nor the GPU
    # itself is exercised. Only a real campaign does that.
    export PATH=/opt/BindCraft2/.venv/bin:$PATH
    bindcraft --help > /dev/null
    python -c "import jax; print('jax', jax.__version__)"
    test -d /opt/bindcraft-weights
    echo "BindCraft2 self-test OK"

%runscript
    exec bindcraft "$@"

%help
    BindCraft2 — de novo binder design. GPU required; there is no CPU mode.

    The entry point is `bindcraft`, so arguments start at the subcommand:

      apptainer run --nv --bind "$PWD":/data bindcraft2-cu13.sif \
          design /data/design.json

    A minimal design.json, with target.pdb beside it:

      {
        "targets": [{"name": "my_target", "target_path": "/data/target.pdb",
                     "chains": "A", "hotspots": "54,56,66-70"}],
        "modality": "binder",
        "binder_lengths": [80, 80],
        "number_of_final_designs": 10,
        "project_folder": "/data/results/my_target"
      }

    Other modalities: --modality VHH (drop binder_lengths, the scaffold sets the length),
    peptide, antibody. List the shipped targets with `design --list-targets`.

    SET workers_per_gpu=1 UNLESS YOU HAVE CHECKED OTHERWISE. workers_per_gpu defaults to
    'auto' and packs two workers onto a 48 GB card; attention_backend defaults to 'auto'
    and picks cuDNN. Both together, the two workers capture cuDNN attention graphs on one
    device and kill each other:

      JaxRuntimeError: INTERNAL: detail::cuda_graph_end_capture(...) failed with
      capturing stream has unjoined work ... [executable_name='jit_sequence_design_loss']

    The campaign does not stop -- the surviving worker finishes it at half throughput and
    the job exits 134. Measured on an L40S: 5 of 7 campaigns lost a worker on the defaults,
    0 of 2 with workers_per_gpu=1, and 0 of 2 with attention_backend=chunked at two
    workers. That last one is what identifies the cause: two workers are fine, cuDNN
    attention from two processes is not.

      bindcraft design campaign.json --set 'workers_per_gpu=1'
      bindcraft design campaign.json --set 'attention_backend=chunked'

    CONFIRM JAX SEES THE CARD BEFORE A LONG CAMPAIGN. JAX warns once and then runs on the
    CPU, which looks like a working job that will never finish:

      apptainer exec --nv bindcraft2-cu13.sif \
          python -c "import jax; print(jax.devices()); assert jax.default_backend()=='gpu'"

    One CudaDevice per card is the answer. [CpuDevice(id=0)] means stop and fix it.

    KEEP THE COMPILED-GRAPH CACHE FOR A SWEEP. Each prediction shape costs about 60 s to
    compile and 1.5 s to read back. This image caches to node-local /tmp, which is lost when
    the job ends. For a campaign series on nodes carrying the same GPU model, point it at
    shared storage instead:

      apptainer run --nv --env JAX_COMPILATION_CACHE_DIR=/shared/path/bc2_xla_cache ...

    Use one cache directory per GPU model: a compiled executable is not portable across
    cards, and mixing them silently defeats the cache.

    MOUNT EVERY TREE YOUR PATHS POINT INTO, including anything a symlink crosses. A
    parameter or target directory that is a link into an unmounted filesystem exists to
    `ls` and not to the campaign, and preflight reports it as missing.

    Weights are baked in: BINDCRAFT_WEIGHTS=/opt/bindcraft-weights is the cache root, and
    the 15 params_*.npz files (monomer, _ptm and _multimer_v3 sets) are one level down in
    /opt/bindcraft-weights/alphafold/. To use a different copy, set BINDCRAFT_AF2_PARAMS to
    a directory holding params_<model>.npz -- that is the alphafold/ level, not its parent.
    It overrides everything.

    Licence: BindCraft2 Source-Available (Hosting-Restricted). Free for any internal use
    including commercial, and redistribution is allowed; what is restricted is offering the
    Software itself to third parties as a hosted or managed service. Providing design
    OUTPUTS (sequences, structures) to others is explicitly permitted. See LICENSE.md.
